# ============================================================================================
# ON 2026-10-02 THIS FILE DELETED THE STUDY.
#
# results/ was listed here as "regenerated by every run, never committed". It was not
# regenerated. It held the only copy of 24 matrices, ~5,900 run records and ~102,000
# gateway records, and when tools/preflight.mjs ran rmSync('results', {recursive:true})
# on a verbatim --out, git had never tracked the directory, so there was nothing to
# restore from. Recycle Bin: 0 matches. Volume Shadow Copies: none. 223 gateway records
# of 102,000 survived, and only because four files were held open by running processes.
#
# THE RULE THAT CAME OUT OF IT:
#   No result may exist only in an untracked directory.
#
# results/ and _ev/ are EVIDENCE, not build output. They are tracked. If a file in one of
# them is too large for plain git it is tracked compressed (see recovered/ below); if it is genuinely
# re-derivable, the exclusion carries the source it is re-derivable from. It does NOT come
# back into this file.
#
# DO NOT ADD results/ OR _ev/ HERE AGAIN.
# ============================================================================================

# ---- Secrets: the only entries here that are not negotiable. ----
.keys.json
.keys.*
*.key
FILL-IN-KEYS.json
credentials*.yml
credentials*.yaml

# ---- The plain-text session transcript: re-derivable from the tracked .gz ----
#
# recovered/sessions-text.txt.gz IS tracked (the redacted transcript, gzip so it fits plain git
# without LFS). The 199 MB plain-text copy is `gunzip -k recovered/sessions-text.txt.gz`.
# tools/recover-from-sessions.mjs also writes the plain file, UNREDACTED, from the raw session
# logs: it captured live API keys once, so it must never be committed. Hence this entry.
recovered/sessions-text.txt

# ---- Third-party Python environments: 367 MB, reproducible from requirements. ----
.venvs/

# ---- Vendored dependencies ----
node_modules/

# ---- results/_scratch: the ONE directory inside results/ that git does not track ----
#
# This is not "results/ is ignored again". Every matrix, every gateway log and every run record
# under results/ is tracked; that is the whole point of the rule at the top of this file.
#
# results/_scratch is the designated scratch root - the single place inside the archive that
# tools/safe-fs.mjs permits a caller to DELETE. Something deletable is by definition not
# evidence, so tracking it is incoherent, and indexing it is actively harmful: on 2026-10-02 a
# browser cache Edge had left open in there made `git add -A results` fail outright with
# "Permission denied" on Cache_Data/data_0, and the backup fail with EBUSY on Cookies. The
# 620-run DeepSeek matrix could not be committed because of a file that did not matter.
#
# Preflight probes, pilots and one-off reproduction runs live here. They are reproducible and
# they are not results. If something in here becomes evidence, move it out of _scratch and it
# is tracked again on the next add - which is exactly the signal you want.
results/_scratch/

# ---- Transient alert output, never evidence ----
#
# tools/credit-alert.mjs used to write its "top this provider up" summary to the repo root. That
# is transient state, not a result, and it has moved into results/_scratch with the other
# transient state. This entry covers the copy an already-running alert window left behind, and
# anything a stale process writes before it is restarted.
#
# It is here rather than deleted because safe-fs.mjs is the only module allowed to delete, and it
# correctly refuses a path that is not a scratch root - a rule worth more than a tidy root.
#
# It is NOT a precedent: results/ and _ev/ stay tracked (see the top of this file).
CREDIT-ALERT.md

# ---- Local scratch ----
# Harness smoke-run leftovers (the launchers were removed in the release cleanup).
.sweagent-smoke/
.tmp-oh-smoke/
.tmp-goose-*/
_goose-smoke/
*.tmp
*~
.DS_Store

# ---- LaTeX build intermediates: regenerated by every build, never evidence ----
#
# paper/PAPER.pdf IS tracked: it is the deliverable the user opens. The rest are re-derived by
# `tectonic PAPER.tex` from PAPER.tex + refs.bib, so only the sources and the PDF are committed.
paper/*.aux
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.xdv
